@startuml 05-sequence-secrets
title FlowAI Platform - Secret Lifecycle (sequence)

autonumber

participant "Operator" as Op
participant "Web UI" as UI
participant "API Gateway" as GW
participant "Secret Service" as SS
participant "Automation" as Auto
participant "Event Router" as ER
participant "Executor" as EX
participant "Agent Container" as AG

note over Op, SS
  GW is an auth-aware reverse proxy. UI -> GW (auth) -> SS.
  GW only does auth + route. No business logic.
  All writes happen in backend services.
end note

== Operator creates secret (write-only at UI/GW) ==

Op -> UI : Open Secrets page
UI -> GW : POST /secrets { bearer_token, name, value, scope }
GW -> GW : Validate bearer_token
GW -> SS : POST /secrets { name, value, scope }
SS -> SS : Encrypt, persist (audit logged)
SS --> GW : 201 secret_id
GW --> UI : 201 secret_id
UI --> Op : Secret saved

note over Auto, EX
  Task time. Automation submits via REST to the Event Router
  with a bearer token from GW.
end note

== Submit (automation -> ER direct) ==

Auto -> GW : POST /auth/login
GW --> Auto : 200 { bearer_token }
Auto -> ER : REST POST /tasks { bearer_token, prompt, tools, secret_ids: [a, b] }
ER -> SS : REST open env (validate secret_ids exist for project)
SS --> ER : ok
ER -> ER : Build scope = HMAC(project_id, task_id, secret_ids, TTL)
ER -> ER : Persist task (incl. scope_token + routing_target) in ER DB
ER --> Auto : 202 task_id

== Dispatch (ER dispatches via REST) ==

ER -> ER : Pick next pending task from ER DB
ER -> EX : REST POST /dispatch { task_spec + scope_token }
EX -> EX : Pull image

== Secret resolve at task start ==

EX -> SS : REST open env { scope_token }
SS -> SS : Validate scope signature, expiry, project
SS --> EX : env-style map { SECRET_A=..., SECRET_B=... }
EX -> AG : Start container, mount env-style keys (env / tmpfs)

note over AG
  Has secrets from start. No runtime fetch needed unless refreshed.
end note

note over AG, EX
  On task end. Container terminated. Scope token expires. Plaintext gone.
end note

@enduml